# Japanese. Machine translated. See es.ftl for the review note: the strings
# that delete, empty or discard are what a native reviewer should read first.
#
# No plural select expressions here, deliberately. Japanese has one grammatical
# number, so CLDR gives it only `other`; a [one] variant would never be
# selected and would only mislead the next translator into thinking it was.
#
# Anything absent falls back to English rather than showing an id, so an
# incomplete file is safe to ship. A wrong one is not.

